Scenario: In a Hospital patient management system, the database is crucial for storing and managing patient information efficiently. Imagine you are a database administrator at a hospital. A new requirement has come in to delete a patient record from the database based on their unique patient ID. You decide to use JDBC to interact with the database. 

Question: In the context of the Hospital patient management system scenario, if you need to delete a patient record from the database using JDBC, which type of statement would you use and why? Provide a code snippet similar to the one below and explain its significance in the given scenario:

```java
PreparedStatement stmt = con.prepareStatement("DELETE FROM patients WHERE patient_id = ?");
stmt.setInt(1, 12345);
int i = stmt.executeUpdate();
System.out.println(i + " record deleted");
```

